<title>UK: Dee Valley has 93 pct of Chester.</title>
<headline>Dee Valley has 93 pct of Chester.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>British water company Dee Valley Water Plc, the holding company for Wrexham Water, owns or has valid acceptances for 93.2 percent of Chester Water Plc's issued share capital, Charterhouse Bank Ltd said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Dee Valley Water has made a recommended offer for Chester Water, valuing it at 20.3 million pounds. Britain's water industry regulator OFWAT has given the merger between Wrexham and Chester Water the go-ahead.</p>
<p>Charterhouse is acting for Dee Valley Water.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
